    "created_at": "2022-10-17T21:37:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-17T21:37:32Z",
    "body": "per my PR @nt1m, that specific bit of the text indicating that the element(s) become \"disabled\" is changing - https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/8122\r\n\r\nDoes this need to change back?  I made the change because of situations where content (form controls) are within an inert subtree but they still need to participate in a form submission.  e.g., a stepped form where different portions of the form are set off-screen and prevented from being accessed when not in view (or partially in view) via the inert attribute.  Those form controls shouldn't be operable / accessible to users so long as they are inert, but they also shouldn't be 'disabled' - unless the term is being used differently in this context?  Am I incorrect on any of my understanding here?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
